<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xingtai</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Xiangguo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xingtai is a city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, at the eastern foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taihang-mountains">Taihang Mountains</a>, and one of the oldest cities of northern China, once the centre of the Zhou-era state of Xing. As Xiangguo it was the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-er">Zhang Er</a>'s kingdom of Changshan in 206 BCE and, from 319 CE, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shi-le">Shi Le</a>'s Later Zhao.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xingtai.jpg" alt="Xingtai" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wcr1993 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Xingtai_Museum_(20220503).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
